---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout current="Writing" title="Writing System | HJH">
  <section class="content-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Writing System</span>
    <h1>Obsidian as the upstream brain</h1>
    <p>Write locally in Obsidian, sync selected folders into Astro content, and publish the static site without giving the website access to your private vault.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="now-grid writing-grid">
    <article>
      <span>01</span>
      <h2>Write in Obsidian</h2>
      <p>Use normal Markdown notes. Frontmatter such as title, description, date, tags, draft, status, abstract, pdf, and code is understood by the sync script.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span>02</span>
      <h2>Sync at build time</h2>
      <p>The Obsidian sync script copies selected Notes and Papers folders from your vault into generated content folders. Drafts stay private unless explicitly enabled.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span>03</span>
      <h2>Publish static pages</h2>
      <p>Astro renders notes, papers, RSS, tags, and search JSON into static files. Cloudflare serves the result; your local vault never has to be public.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span>04</span>
      <h2>Keep Git clean</h2>
      <p>For public notes, commit the generated Markdown. For private vaults, keep the vault path local and only publish what the sync script exports.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
